[{"data":1,"prerenderedAt":1648},["ShallowReactive",2],{"docs-page-fr-\u002Fremote-control":3,"docs-nav-fr":244},{"id":4,"title":5,"body":6,"description":235,"extension":236,"meta":237,"navigation":238,"order":239,"path":240,"seo":241,"stem":242,"__hash__":243},"content_fr\u002Fremote-control.md","Contrôle à distance",{"type":7,"value":8,"toc":226},"minimark",[9,13,17,22,57,60,64,101,105,126,129,133,166,170,176],[10,11,5],"h1",{"id":12},"contrôle-à-distance",[14,15,16],"p",{},"SoundNinja peut écouter sur ton réseau local pour que Bitfocus Companion (ou n’importe quel client HTTP\u002FWebSocket) joue et arrête des sons.",[18,19,21],"h2",{"id":20},"activer-le-serveur-distant","Activer le serveur distant",[23,24,25,34,40,47],"ol",{},[26,27,28,29,33],"li",{},"Ouvre ",[30,31,32],"strong",{},"Paramètres → Distant",".",[26,35,36,37,33],{},"Active le serveur distant. Le port par défaut est ",[30,38,39],{},"7331",[26,41,42,43,33],{},"Optionnel : définis un token. Les clients doivent l’envoyer comme Bearer token ou ",[44,45,46],"code",{},"?token=",[26,48,49,50,53,54,33],{},"Copie l’URL ",[44,51,52],{},"http:\u002F\u002FIP:PORT",", ou copie l’IP système depuis ",[30,55,56],{},"Paramètres → À propos",[14,58,59],{},"Windows peut afficher une invite pare-feu la première fois que le serveur démarre. Autorise l’accès au réseau privé.",[18,61,63],{"id":62},"bitfocus-companion","Bitfocus Companion",[23,65,66,75,84,94],{},[26,67,68,69,33],{},"Installe ",[70,71,63],"a",{"href":72,"rel":73},"https:\u002F\u002Fbitfocus.io\u002Fcompanion",[74],"nofollow",[26,76,77,78,83],{},"Télécharge ",[70,79,82],{"href":80,"rel":81},"https:\u002F\u002Fgithub.com\u002Fmarcus-universe\u002FSoundNinja\u002Freleases\u002Flatest\u002Fdownload\u002FSoundNinja-Companion.tgz",[74],"SoundNinja-Companion.tgz",". Il n’y a pas encore de paquet Companion Store.",[26,85,86,87,90,91,33],{},"Dans Companion : ",[30,88,89],{},"Modules → Load module package"," et choisis le ",[44,92,93],{},".tgz",[26,95,96,97,100],{},"Ajoute une connexion ",[30,98,99],{},"Sound Ninja",". Colle l’IP du PC, le port, et le token si tu en as défini un.",[18,102,104],{"id":103},"actions","Actions",[106,107,108,114,120],"ul",{},[26,109,110,113],{},[30,111,112],{},"Trigger Sound"," — choisis dans le menu déroulant live, ou tape un ID de son de 8 caractères (les variables Companion marchent)",[26,115,116,119],{},[30,117,118],{},"Stop Sound"," — arrête un son en lecture par ID",[26,121,122,125],{},[30,123,124],{},"Stop All"," — arrête tous les sons en lecture",[14,127,128],{},"Copie un ID de son dans SoundNinja depuis le menu contextuel du bouton ou la puce d’ID de la sélection multiple.",[18,130,132],{"id":131},"feedbacks-et-variables","Feedbacks et variables",[106,134,135,141,154,160],{},[26,136,137,140],{},[30,138,139],{},"Sound Playing"," — vrai tant que cet ID de son est actif (utilise-le pour la couleur du bouton)",[26,142,143,146,147,150,151],{},[44,144,145],{},"$(soundninja:connected)"," — ",[44,148,149],{},"true"," \u002F ",[44,152,153],{},"false",[26,155,156,159],{},[44,157,158],{},"$(soundninja:playing_count)"," — combien de sons jouent",[26,161,162,165],{},[44,163,164],{},"$(soundninja:last_triggered)"," — dernier ID de son déclenché",[18,167,169],{"id":168},"api-http-avancé","API HTTP (avancé)",[14,171,172,173],{},"Chemin de base : ",[44,174,175],{},"\u002Fapi\u002Fv1",[106,177,178,184,190,196,206,212,220],{},[26,179,180,183],{},[44,181,182],{},"GET \u002Finfo"," — nom de l’app, version, protocole, si un token est requis",[26,185,186,189],{},[44,187,188],{},"GET \u002Fsounds"," — liste des sons (id, name, tabs, active)",[26,191,192,195],{},[44,193,194],{},"GET \u002Fstate"," — sons plus IDs actuellement en lecture",[26,197,198,201,202,205],{},[44,199,200],{},"POST \u002Ftrigger"," avec ",[44,203,204],{},"{ \"id\" }"," — jouer un son",[26,207,208,211],{},[44,209,210],{},"GET \u002Ftrigger\u002F:id"," — jouer (facile à tester dans un navigateur)",[26,213,214,201,217,219],{},[44,215,216],{},"POST \u002Fstop",[44,218,204],{}," optionnel — arrêter un son ou tous",[26,221,222,225],{},[44,223,224],{},"GET \u002Fws"," — état en direct ; envoyer des commandes trigger\u002Fstop en entrée",{"title":227,"searchDepth":228,"depth":228,"links":229},"",2,[230,231,232,233,234],{"id":20,"depth":228,"text":21},{"id":62,"depth":228,"text":63},{"id":103,"depth":228,"text":104},{"id":131,"depth":228,"text":132},{"id":168,"depth":228,"text":169},"Déclencher SoundNinja depuis Bitfocus Companion sur le réseau local.","md",{},true,7,"\u002Fremote-control",{"title":5,"description":235},"remote-control","J79_grc3VOlT-VyYh-0m1UJi4l-Yax0za7DQZ5iZpxw",[245,372,573,720,1123,1258,1405,1551],{"id":246,"title":247,"body":248,"description":365,"extension":236,"meta":366,"navigation":238,"order":367,"path":368,"seo":369,"stem":370,"__hash__":371},"content_fr\u002Foverview.md","Aperçu",{"type":7,"value":249,"toc":359},[250,253,256,259,262,266,280,284,322,326,335,339],[10,251,247],{"id":252},"aperçu",[14,254,255],{},"SoundNinja est un soundboard open source pour le live streaming, les discussions entre amis et l’enregistrement de podcasts. Il est construit avec Tauri v2 et Nuxt 4 pour rester léger en RAM et sur le disque.",[14,257,258],{},"Le but est simple : garder une énorme bibliothèque de sons facile à parcourir, puis jouer le bon clip en quelques millisecondes. L’interface marche aussi comme tableau de bord en VR.",[14,260,261],{},"SoundNinja est encore en développement précoce. Les fonctions marchent, mais toutes les plateformes ne sont pas entièrement testées.",[18,263,265],{"id":264},"pour-qui","Pour qui",[106,267,268,271,274,277],{},[26,269,270],{},"Les streameurs qui ont besoin de cues sonores instantanés",[26,272,273],{},"Les amis qui veulent un board partagé pour le vocal",[26,275,276],{},"Les podcasteurs qui enregistrent des clips et les posent sur un board",[26,278,279],{},"Quiconque veut un soundboard personnalisable et local-first",[18,281,283],{"id":282},"ce-que-tu-peux-faire","Ce que tu peux faire",[106,285,286,289,292,295,298,301,304,307,310,316,319],{},[26,287,288],{},"Construire un soundboard à partir de tes propres fichiers audio",[26,290,291],{},"Organiser les sons dans des onglets colorés, des groupes, des tags et la recherche",[26,293,294],{},"Filtrer par tags (OU) et trier par nom, date, durée ou taille",[26,296,297],{},"Sélection multiple avec rectangle ou plage Maj, puis couleur, déplacement ou suppression en lot",[26,299,300],{},"Régler le volume par son depuis le menu contextuel",[26,302,303],{},"Concevoir le look avec le Theme Creator",[26,305,306],{},"Enregistrer l’audio du PC ou un micro dans le Record Editor",[26,308,309],{},"Assigner des raccourcis à des sons individuels",[26,311,312,313],{},"Déclencher des sons depuis ",[70,314,63],{"href":315},"\u002Fdocs\u002Fremote-control",[26,317,318],{},"Importer et exporter un soundboard complet pour le partager",[26,320,321],{},"Utiliser des GIF ou des images sur les boutons — bibliothèque de dossiers locale ou KLIPY",[18,323,325],{"id":324},"licence","Licence",[14,327,328,329,334],{},"SoundNinja est un logiciel libre sous ",[70,330,333],{"href":331,"rel":332},"https:\u002F\u002Fgithub.com\u002Fmarcus-universe\u002FSoundNinja\u002Fblob\u002Fmain\u002FLICENSE",[74],"GPL-3.0",". Forke-le, modifie-le, partage-le.",[18,336,338],{"id":337},"prochaines-étapes","Prochaines étapes",[23,340,341,347,353],{},[26,342,343],{},[70,344,346],{"href":345},"\u002Fdocs\u002Finstallation","Installer SoundNinja",[26,348,349],{},[70,350,352],{"href":351},"\u002Fdocs\u002Fadding-sounds","Ajouter des sons",[26,354,355],{},[70,356,358],{"href":357},"\u002Fdocs\u002Forganizing-sounds","Organiser ton board",{"title":227,"searchDepth":228,"depth":228,"links":360},[361,362,363,364],{"id":264,"depth":228,"text":265},{"id":282,"depth":228,"text":283},{"id":324,"depth":228,"text":325},{"id":337,"depth":228,"text":338},"Ce qu’est SoundNinja et ce que tu peux en faire.",{},1,"\u002Foverview",{"title":247,"description":365},"overview","nBakDXsUbMnm0zyn8m6jAooziqocGWiZV3EwAtrg0xk",{"id":373,"title":374,"body":375,"description":568,"extension":236,"meta":569,"navigation":238,"order":228,"path":570,"seo":571,"stem":379,"__hash__":572},"content_fr\u002Finstallation.md","Installation",{"type":7,"value":376,"toc":561},[377,380,394,398,419,422,426,440,443,447,471,482,486,493,497,512,542,557],[10,378,374],{"id":379},"installation",[14,381,382,383,387,388,393],{},"Récupère un build sur la ",[70,384,386],{"href":385},"\u002Fdownload","page Télécharger"," ou sur ",[70,389,392],{"href":390,"rel":391},"https:\u002F\u002Fgithub.com\u002Fmarcus-universe\u002FSoundNinja\u002Freleases\u002Flatest",[74],"GitHub Releases",". SoundNinja est en développement précoce — traite les builds comme des bêtas.",[18,395,397],{"id":396},"windows","Windows",[106,399,400,410,413,416],{},[26,401,402,405,406,409],{},[30,403,404],{},"Installateur (.exe)"," ou ",[30,407,408],{},"MSI (.msi)"," pour Windows 64 bits",[26,411,412],{},"Cible de la landing page : Windows 10 et plus",[26,414,415],{},"Le README de l’app mentionne aussi Windows 8 et supérieur",[26,417,418],{},"L’installateur NSIS est sombre. Choisis une langue à l’installation — SoundNinja la retient au prochain lancement.",[14,420,421],{},"Lance l’installateur, puis ouvre SoundNinja depuis le menu Démarrer.",[18,423,425],{"id":424},"macos","macOS",[106,427,428,434,437],{},[26,429,430,433],{},[30,431,432],{},".dmg universel"," pour Apple Silicon et Intel",[26,435,436],{},"Cible de la landing page : macOS 10.14 et plus",[26,438,439],{},"Le README de l’app mentionne macOS 10.15 et supérieur",[14,441,442],{},"Ouvre l’image disque et glisse SoundNinja dans Applications.",[18,444,446],{"id":445},"linux","Linux",[106,448,449,455,461,468],{},[26,450,451,454],{},[30,452,453],{},"Debian (.deb)"," pour Ubuntu \u002F Debian",[26,456,457,460],{},[30,458,459],{},"AppImage"," pour les autres distros",[26,462,463,464,467],{},"Après publication d’une release, les utilisateurs Arch peuvent installer ",[44,465,466],{},"soundninja-bin"," depuis l’AUR",[26,469,470],{},"Testé sur Ubuntu 20.04",[14,472,473,474,477,478,481],{},"Les builds desktop ont besoin des paquets WebKit et GTK. Sous Debian\u002FUbuntu, ça veut souvent dire ",[44,475,476],{},"libwebkit2gtk",", ",[44,479,480],{},"libgtk-3-0"," et une bibliothèque app-indicator.",[18,483,485],{"id":484},"mises-à-jour","Mises à jour",[14,487,488,489,492],{},"Dans l’app, ouvre ",[30,490,491],{},"Aide → Rechercher les mises à jour",". Tu peux aussi laisser SoundNinja vérifier au démarrage dans les Paramètres.",[18,494,496],{"id":495},"compiler-depuis-les-sources","Compiler depuis les sources",[14,498,499,500,505,506,511],{},"Besoin d’un build custom ? Clone ",[70,501,504],{"href":502,"rel":503},"https:\u002F\u002Fgithub.com\u002Fmarcus-universe\u002FSoundNinja",[74],"le repo",", installe les ",[70,507,510],{"href":508,"rel":509},"https:\u002F\u002Fv2.tauri.app\u002Fstart\u002Fprerequisites\u002F",[74],"prérequis Tauri",", puis :",[513,514,518],"pre",{"className":515,"code":516,"language":517,"meta":227,"style":227},"language-bash shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark","bun install\nbun run tauri:serve\n","bash",[44,519,520,532],{"__ignoreMap":227},[521,522,524,528],"span",{"class":523,"line":367},"line",[521,525,527],{"class":526},"sScJk","bun",[521,529,531],{"class":530},"sZZnC"," install\n",[521,533,534,536,539],{"class":523,"line":228},[521,535,527],{"class":526},[521,537,538],{"class":530}," run",[521,540,541],{"class":530}," tauri:serve\n",[14,543,544,477,547,405,550,553,554,33],{},[44,545,546],{},"npm",[44,548,549],{},"pnpm",[44,551,552],{},"deno"," marchent aussi. Build de production : ",[44,555,556],{},"bun run tauri:build",[558,559,560],"style",{},"html pre.shiki code .sScJk, html code.shiki .sScJk{--shiki-default:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0}html pre.shiki code .sZZnC, html code.shiki .sZZnC{--shiki-default:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF}html .default .shiki span {color: